From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:54:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 268/342] dwc2: two isochronous OUT streams behind a hub

All OUT streams started in microframe 0. A 48 kHz stereo packet is two
start-splits in a row, and a translator takes those with nothing between them:
of two adapters playing behind one hub (these hubs run one translator for all
their ports), both lost their packets. A tone on one of them came back through
a cable with half of its time silent. The second OUT stream on a hub now starts
in microframe 4, clear of the first and of the IN start-splits of microframe 2.
A third is refused with B_BUSY: it would break the other two.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
